  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating and comparing the variance of the two lotteries and preferring the one with lower variance. The individual did not mention variance, nor did they refer to the spread or dispersion of outcomes. Instead, their reasoning focused on the high probability of receiving 0 Euros, the magnitude of the potential loss, and the desire to avoid a loss. Although the variance-based reason leads to the same choice (Lottery B), the individual’s justification does not align with the rule of minimizing variance. Their deliberation process was based on loss aversion and perceived likelihood of no loss, not on statistical variance. Therefore, while the outcome coincides, the reasoning process is different. The individual did not use the variance-based reason to make the decision. The assessment is not certain, but the absence of any reference to variance or spread, and the presence of loss-avoidance reasoning, strongly suggests the reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
}

